SUZANNE KAO: Sure.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.870
So a typical scenario that we
really see that I think really

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.840
captures why something like a,
quote, "tool" like this would

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:55.360
be really useful is, for
instance, an aerospace

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.760
and defense client.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.780
So if you have an aerospace
and defense client,

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:01.930
if you're familiar with export
controls, a lot of their data

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:03.610
